# Test Standards

- Cover behavior changes with focused unit/integration/architecture tests.
- Keep tests deterministic and reproducible; avoid time/random/network flakiness.
- Prefer fixtures and VCR cassettes for external API interactions.
- Validate explicit contracts and invariants (schemas, modes, run types, boundaries).
- For changed public behavior, add regression tests before or with implementation.
- Use project command style when suggesting runs: `uv run python -m pytest ...`.
- Do not weaken assertions to make tests pass; preserve contract-level intent.
